General


Using dropdown for units keeps usability clean, and lessens security risk of injection. Not just specifically for this challenge, but trying to keep that mindset as a whole.

In converter.js, UNIT_CATEGORY is a lookup dictionary. Give it a unit key like 'KELVIN' gives back 'TEMPERATURE'.It basically checks if two units are in the same family.LITERS_PER_UNIT is the same for volume.

Object.freeze(...) just prevents any other code from accidentally mutating these tables at runtime — it's a safety habit, not logic.

Every calculation input converts to Kelvin, then converts out of it because kelvin is the international base unit of measurement for temperature.
Every liquid calculation input converts through Liters. (Ex. converting cups to gallons is actually "cups → liters, then liters →
gallons" under the hood. ). This keeps the combo calculations small and not having a different formula for each conversion combination




