roundtotenth
math.round only rounds to whole numbers. Claude multiplied by 10 first which shifts the tenths unit to the ones, use math.round, then divide by 10

The + Number.EPSILON is for edge cases - (a tiny fixed constant, about 2.22e-16) is a defensive nudge against a specific floating-point quirk: numbers like 0.1 + 0.2 aren't stored exactly in binary floating point, so a value that's mathematically exactly X.X5 can sometimes be stored as X.X49999... and round the wrong way. Adding an infinitesimally small amount nudges those edge cases back onto the correct side before rounding. It doesn't affect any normal-sized value in any visible way.

